<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Louis returns one week after intake and is seen by Dr. Featherstone-Ibe of addiction psychiatry on the same day. He has used no cocaine since three days before his intake visit, ten days in all, and has kept his naloxone and test strips at home. The belief that people are following him and plan to harm him is less intense but still there; he checks the street from his window several times a night and sleeps about four hours. He has had no hallucinations and no thoughts of harming himself or anyone else, and he has not confronted anyone. The phone check three days after intake found him safe. The intake urine test, done with his consent, was positive for cocaine and negative for fentanyl, other opioids, amphetamines, benzodiazepines and cannabis. HIV, hepatitis C and syphilis tests were negative; he is not infected with hepatitis B and is not immune. His thyroid and vitamin B12 tests were normal. His brain MRI this morning showed no contusion, microbleeds or other abnormality. He wants to get well and agreed to the specialist plan. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Last cocaine use</td><td>Ten days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Persecutory beliefs</td><td>Present, less intense; partial insight</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About four hours</td></tr><tr><td>Intake results</td><td>Urine positive for cocaine, negative for fentanyl and other drugs; HIV, hepatitis C and syphilis negative; hepatitis B not immune; TSH and B12 normal</td></tr><tr><td>Brain MRI</td><td>Normal for age</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

